        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your patient, a 67-year-old male, who presented on 15/02/2026 with worsening dyspnoea, increased sputum production and reduced exercise tolerance consistent with an acute exacerbation of his known COPD. On admission, oxygen saturation was reduced at 88% on room air. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed type II respiratory failure. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with controlled oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and prophylactic antibiotics. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 16/02/2026 with an oral steroid taper, inhaler optimisation, and referral for pulmonary rehabilitation. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks.</div>"
            },
